.TH "SONGMEAN.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
songmean.sh \- search for an explanation of the current Spotify song
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBsongmean.sh [BROWSER]\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the current Spotify track artist and title through go\-playerctl (or playerctl as fallback), build a Perplexity search for lyrics, meaning, context and analysis, and open it in a browser. An explicit browser argument takes priority over BROWSER; otherwise select a detected browser.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBBROWSER\fR
Browser command used if no browser argument is supplied.
.SH NOTES
When the browser argument is chrome, the helper resolves an available Chrome/Chromium executable. A browser must be installed.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires Spotify metadata via go-playerctl or playerctl and
a working browser; the search itself requires network access.
.SH OPERATION
An explicit browser argument takes precedence over BROWSER.
Without either, the script searches Konqueror, Firefox, Chrome
variants and xdg-open in that order. The browser alias chrome
resolves to an installed Chrome/Chromium executable. The script
URL-encodes artist and title with a lyrics, meaning, context
and analysis query, and opens Perplexity in that browser.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
songmean.sh
songmean.sh firefox
BROWSER=konqueror songmean.sh
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
Missing metadata may mean Spotify is stopped or the selected
player helper cannot query the track. BROWSER must name a
single executable, not a compound shell command. The tool
opens an external search and does not analyse songs offline.
.SH SEE ALSO
go\-playerctl(1), playerctl(1)
